{"availability":"available","full":"Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp","name":"guard-core-mcp","description":"MCP server for the Guard ecosystem — config validation, docs search and live threat detection for fastapi-guard, guard-core and guard-agent. Answers from the versions installed in your project, not from a model's memory.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-25T11:12:50Z","updated":"2026-10-09T21:55:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://guard-core.github.io/guard-core-mcp/","topics":["api-security","developer-tools","fastapi","python","security"],"demo":"https://playground.guard-core.com/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.875Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.875Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.875Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.875Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Guard Core is the Python engine. Framework adapters are thin wrappers that translate native request/response types into Guard Core's protocols. The telemetry agents ship security events and metrics to the monitoring backend. Parallel engine implementations exist for Go, PHP, TypeScript (on npm), and Rust (on crates.io) - all ports of the same reference semantics, conformance-tested against the shared adversarial corpus.","This server answers those from the installed package: real pydantic validation, real field metadata, and the real detection engine. It also answers the cross-language questions the libraries cannot answer: which package guards a Gin, Fastify, Laravel or Rocket app, whether it is tagged or still path-dependent, how to wire its telemetry agent, and what response codes the SaaS ingest endpoint returns."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"58644daacfe2e027e861371af19020fb032afa8aeae44febf410cebdb62f4264","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.978Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.978Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Guard Core is the Python engine. Framework adapters are thin wrappers that translate native request/response types into Guard Core's protocols. The telemetry agents ship security events and metrics to the monitoring backend. Parallel engine implementations exist for Go, PHP, TypeScript (on npm), and Rust (on crates.io) - all ports of the same reference semantics, conformance-tested against the shared adversarial corpus.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The same tools are also served remotely at and packaged as a ChatGPT plugin: sign in with a guard-core account, and ChatGPT can validate configs, search the docs and run payloads through the hosted detection engine (the latest published releases, not your local versions).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"58644daacfe2e027e861371af19020fb032afa8aeae44febf410cebdb62f4264","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.978Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T21:55:06Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Guard-Core/guard-core-mcp/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:46.979Z","hash":"58644daacfe2e027e861371af19020fb032afa8aeae44febf410cebdb62f4264","originalBytes":14116,"storedBytes":14116,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["adapter","agent","crates.io","npm","package","pypi","engine","packagist","release","telemetry","core","guard","config","guardcore","published","role","what","docs","guard-core","guard-core-mcp","plugin","agents","answers","chatgpt","documentation","ecosystem","full","production-ready.","real","search","server","which","detection","environment","exist","fastify","g